# WHAT DOES NOT GO ON THE PUBLIC SITE.
#
# Vercel deploys the repository as-is, so anything committed here is served at
# its own URL whether it is part of the site or not. That is how
# VERCEL-SETUP.md — the deploy runbook, GitHub-token instructions included —
# came to be readable at https://<domain>/VERCEL-SETUP.md. It was not linked
# from anywhere, which is not the same as being private.
#
# This file is the deployment's own boundary and is separate from .gitignore on
# purpose: .gitignore decides what is worth version-controlling, this decides
# what strangers can fetch. The QA harnesses and the setup notes are worth
# keeping and are not worth publishing.

# the deploy runbook and the repo notes — for whoever works on this, not for readers
VERCEL-SETUP.md
README.md

# the Playwright harnesses. They import a browser driver and assert against a
# local server; on the public site they are dead weight at best.
*.mjs
.tools/

# never part of a static deploy
node_modules/
_to_delete/
.DS_Store
